---
// D-10 (04-08 Task 3): /privacy — v1's current text (915tldr.com2/app/pages/privacy.vue) carried
// over verbatim, converted from Vue/Tailwind template markup to plain semantic HTML inside the
// same narrow reading column as about.astro/contact.astro. Decorative-only markup (background
// noise texture, divider icons, drop-cap letter spans) is dropped — the drop-cap's own letter is
// reunited with the rest of its sentence. "Last Updated · December 2025" is v1's own static text,
// not a computed value, so it is copied as-is rather than recomputed.
//
// 06-07 (D-11, T-06-26): the analytics section is corrected against Umami's own documentation
// (fetched 2026-10-04: https://docs.umami.is/docs/faq, /docs/metric-definitions, /docs/sessions —
// cited in full in docs/phase-06/spanish-pages-review.md). Two prior claims were FALSE and are
// replaced: (1) "Cloudflare for hosting and basic analytics" named the wrong tool — analytics are
// Umami, not Cloudflare; (2) "Your location is your business. We never track where you are." is
// false — Umami's Location metrics record a coarse country/region derived from the request IP
// (metric-definitions: "Location metrics come from different sources depending on the headers.
// The IP address sending the request is used to gather these metrics, but is never stored.").
// Everything else on this page (cookies, no PII, third-party content) is unchanged from 04-08.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy - 915 TLDR"
  description="Privacy policy for 915 TLDR news aggregator. How we handle your data and protect your privacy."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <div data-contact-column>
    <p data-eyebrow>Last Updated · December 2025</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p data-lede>
      Your privacy matters. Here's exactly how we handle (and don't handle) your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Our Promise</h2>
    <p>
      915 TLDR is built with privacy as a core principle, not an afterthought. We believe you
      should be able to read local news without being tracked, profiled, or targeted. That's why
      we've designed this site to collect the absolute minimum data possible.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use Umami, a self-hosted, cookieless analytics tool we run ourselves — it never
      identifies you individually. We don't sell data because we don't collect data worth
      selling. It's that simple.
    </p>

    <h2>What We Don't Collect</h2>
    <p>Privacy by design means saying no to unnecessary data</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>No Personal Data</dt>
      <dd>We don't collect names, emails, or any personally identifiable information.</dd>
      <dt>Coarse Location Only</dt>
      <dd>
        We don't track your precise location. Our analytics record only a coarse, aggregate
        country and region derived from your IP address — the IP address itself is never stored.
      </dd>
      <dt>Minimal Cookies</dt>
      <dd>Only essential cookies for site functionality—theme preference and session.</dd>
      <dt>No Ads or Trackers</dt>
      <dd>Zero third-party advertising or social media tracking scripts.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Third Parties</h2>
    <h3>Cloudflare</h3>
    <p>We use Cloudflare for hosting and content delivery. Their privacy policy applies to their services.</p>
    <h3>Umami Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      We run our own analytics, Umami, self-hosted by 915website.com — your visits are never sent to a third party.
      Umami's tracking code uses no cookies. For
      each page view it records the page and referrer URL, your browser, operating system, device
      type and screen size, your browser's language setting, and a coarse country and region
      computed from your IP address at the moment of the request — the IP address itself is never
      stored. See{' '}
      <a
        href="https://docs.umami.is/docs/metric-definitions"
        rel="noopener external"
        target="_blank"
      >
        Umami's own documentation
        <svg
          data-new-tab-icon
          aria-hidden="true"
          focusable="false"
          width="12"
          height="12"
          viewBox="0 0 12 12"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.1"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
        >
          <path d="M5 1H1v10h10V7" />
          <path d="M7 1h4v4" />
          <path d="M11 1 5 7" />
        </svg>
        <span data-new-tab-cue data-visually-hidden> (opens in a new tab)</span>
      </a>{' '}
      for the complete list.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prefer not to be counted? You can
      <a href="/opt-out">turn analytics off for this browser</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Content</h2>
    <p>
      All news content is sourced from third-party publishers. We link to original articles and do
      not claim ownership of the content. Each article clearly displays its source.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions About Privacy?</h2>
    <p>We're happy to explain anything in more detail. Reach out anytime.</p>
    <p><a href="/contact">Contact Us</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
